    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Deputy-Director--New-Hampshire-Institute-of-Politics_R1682": {
      "title": "Deputy Director, New Hampshire Institute of Politics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a dynamic Deputy Director for the New Hampshire Institute of Politics (NHIOP).  Reporting to the Executive Director of the NHIOP, the Deputy Director oversees the strategic, financial, supervisory, communications, and institutional leadership responsibilities. Programming, Communication and External Relations Identify strategic programming and funding opportunities Manage the overall planning, coordination and oversight of Institute programming including program selections to ensure quality and consistency while considering Institute priorities and coordinating with campus and community partners Oversee the Institute's public relations, branding, and communications, including press releases, Institute speeches, and newsletters while maintaining quality, tone, and consistency Manage speaker, special guests and donor recruitment, invitations, and correspondence to ensure a continued partnership and a positive guest experience Build and maintain relationships with authors, journalists, elected officials, publishers, community partners, special guests and vendors Coordinate the publication of Survey Center poll releases and materials, including press releases, reports, media advisories, website content, and social media Plan special events and programs in conjunction with Institute team Execute special projects as assigned by the Executive Director Maintain records of Institute traditions, events, policies, operating protocols, reference materials, exhibits, polling history, institutional archives and historical collections Leadership & Staff Supervision Provide direct supervision and performance management of the Program Assistant Oversee work planning, prioritization, and delegation of all Institute administrative responsibilities Coordinate administrative support between the Institute and the Politics Department (as managed by the faculty department chair and the Program Assistant) Oversee student interns and student intern projects with assistance from the Program Assistant Financial Management & Oversight Oversee the Institutes financial planning and forecasting of the annual operating expenses, budget development and monitoring and reporting and analysis Execute and monitor polling budgets, contracts, and consultant payments  Partner with the Finance Office on Institute finances and budgeting Qualifications Bachelor's degree preferred, along with a minimum of seven to ten years of experience in the area of public relations/communications, business and/or politics Highly motivated self-starter who takes initiative and is driven to achieve results Ability to collaborate with campus partners and external agencies and constituencies organizing and implementing Institute events and programs Attention to detail, strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines Demonstrated experience in brand management, public relations and strategic communications in a higher education, civic, nonprofit, public policy or political environment.  Supervisory and/or management experience with demonstrated ability to foster a collaborative team environment Enthusiastic, reliable team player with a commitment to excellence in customer service and professionalism Excellent written and interpersonal communication skills Budget experience preferred but not necessary Availability to work occasional evening and weekend hours for special programs or events In order to be considered for this position, please submit both a resume and a cover letter. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Annual-Giving-Coordinator_R1665": {
      "title": "Annual Giving Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a Catholic, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a highly skilled, self-motivated Annual Giving Coordinator to join the College Advancement team. Reporting directly to the Assistant Vice President of Annual Giving, the Annual Giving Coordinator will support the planning, execution, and administration of the College's annual giving program and fundraising initiatives. BASIC FUNCTION The Annual Giving Coordinator provides administrative and operational support for the Office of Annual Giving and serves as a key member of the Advancement team. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Annual Giving, this position works closely with the Associate Director of Annual Giving, Senior Associate Director of Annual Giving, and other Advancement colleagues to support fundraising initiatives, donor engagement efforts, stewardship activities, volunteer programs, and special projects. Serving as the primary point of contact for the Annual Giving office, the Coordinator manages a variety of administrative functions that contribute to the successful execution of annual giving strategies and programs. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong organizational skills, attention to detail, excellent customer service, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative environment. This position maintains regular interaction with alumni, donors, volunteers, students, faculty, staff, and campus partners and may require occasional evening and weekend work in support of College Advancement activities and events. CHARACTERISTIC DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as the primary point of contact for the Office of Annual Giving, responding to email and phone inquiries. Provide administrative support to the Assistant Vice President of Annual Giving, and the Annual Giving team. Support the implementation of annual giving initiatives, donor engagement activities, stewardship efforts, and special projects. Maintain accurate donor and constituent records, including the entry of contact reports and other constituent information. Generate reports, lists, and data exports to support fundraising activities and departmental operations. Assist with donor communications, mailings, appeals, and other fundraising activities. Provide logistical and administrative support for events, meetings, and volunteer activities. Assist with budget administration, invoice processing, expense tracking, and financial reconciliation. Coordinate student workers and provide general office management support. Collaborate with Advancement colleagues and campus partners to support departmental goals and priorities. Attend and support Advancement events and activities as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree preferred. One to three years of experience in fundraising, annual giving, alumni relations, advancement services, higher education, nonprofit development, or a related field preferred. Experience with Blackbaud Raiser's Edge, or similar donor database systems preferred. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Excel, Word, and Outlook. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, deadlines, and budgets simultaneously. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical skills and attention to detail, particularly in data management and reporting. Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive donor information with professionalism and discretion. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced team environment. Positive attitude and exceptional customer service skills, with demonstrated ability to engage professionally with donors, alumni, faculty, staff, students, and volunteers. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends in support of College events and fundraising activities. Successful candidates will be able to assist the College in furthering its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Library-Technical-Assistant---Circulation_R1688-1": {
      "title": "Library Technical Assistant - Circulation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nGeisel Library at Saint Anselm College, a private liberal arts college in the Benedictine Catholic tradition, seeks multiple part-time Circulation Desk Supervisors to join their team. Currently shifts are available on Friday and Monday evenings as below during the fall 2026 and spring 2027 semesters with the occasional option of other shifts as needed: Friday 4:00 pm - 11:00 pm Monday 4:00 pm - 12:00 am Interested candidates should complete the online application and be certain to include a Resume, Cover letter, and 3 References.   Job duties The Circulation Supervisor is responsible for supervising all Circulation Desk operations during assigned hours. This person performs a variety of duties including: assisting library users (students, faculty, staff, guests) with a variety of Circulation Desk needs; supervising Circulation Desk student-assistants; monitoring building conditions and security; maintaining adherence to Circulation policies; working on special projects as assigned; and completing daily shift reports, and closing the library each evening and readying the building for use the next day. Additional hours may be possible throughout the year.   Required skills Exceptional level of attendance and dependability, including during inclement weather Exceptional customer service abilities and interpersonal skills Ability to address patron concerns and difficulties with tact, courtesy, and sound judgment Ability to communicate effectively with college students and to supervise student workers Ability to work autonomously and successfully with limited direct daily supervision Strong office and computer skills and the ability to learn new procedures Reliability in performing daily tasks/duties as assigned Ability to consider occasional assistance with coverage of other shifts (optional) Ability to lift 30 lbs.   Required Experience Associate’s degree or 2 years of college plus 1 – 2 years of relevant experience, or the equivalent combination of education, experience, and maturity.    Desired Experience Some supervisory experience Library Circulation Desk experience Experience working with automated library computer systems and/or contemporary interfaces. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Clinical-Nursing-Faculty--Jean-School-of-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences--Medical-Surgical-Nursing-_R1700": {
      "title": "Clinical Nursing Faculty, Jean School of Nursing and Health Sciences (Medical Surgical Nursing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Jean School of Nursing and Health Sciences at Saint Anselm College invites applications for a full-time Clinical Faculty position in medical surgical nursing to begin in January, 2027. The successful candidate will teach nursing students both in the classroom and clinical setting.  Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae via the college website to the attention of Dr. Carrie E. MacLeod, Director of Undergraduate Nursing.  Prior to interview, three letters of recommendation and academic transcripts will be required.  Applications will be reviewed as they are received and until the position is filled.      Required Skills:   A Master’s degree is required, a Ph.D. is preferred. Ph.D. prepared applicants, or applicants enrolled in a doctoral program, may be considered for a tenure-track position. All candidates should have nursing education teaching experience, and demonstrate clinical expertise in the care of the adult patient.  Candidates should also demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level.   Successful candidates will be able to assist the college in advancing its mission and strategic priorities , which includes institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness .   Come join a team that is preparing future nursing and health care leaders for successful career and life outcomes.  At Saint Anselm College, students develop critical-thinking skills, ethical decision-making, and a humanistic approach to patient care and community challenges.   Founded in 1889, Saint Anselm College is a four-year liberal arts college providing a 21st century education in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. Located in the   greater Boston region in southern New Hampshire, Saint Anselm is well known for its strong liberal arts curriculum, the New Hampshire Institute of Politics, commitment to inclusiveness, a highly successful nursing program,   and a legacy of community service."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Accounts-Payable-Manager_R1699": {
      "title": "Accounts Payable Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a Catholic liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, invites applications for the position of Accounts Payable Manager. Reporting to the Controller, the Accounts Payable Manager is responsible for the accurate and timely processing of accounts payable transactions and employee expense reimbursements while providing excellent customer service to faculty, staff, students, and suppliers The ideal candidate is detail-oriented, highly organized, collaborative, and comfortable working in a fast-paced higher education environment. This position plays a key role in maintaining strong internal controls and supporting the College’s financial operations through the effective use of Workday. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Process invoices, check requests, and payment transactions in a timely and accurate manner using Workday. Ensure proper approvals, coding, and supporting documentation for all disbursements Review and process employee expense reports in accordance with College policies and IRS regulations. Coordinate with purchasing to maintain supplier records, including W-9 documentation and payment setup. Reconcile year-end accounts payable data to accurately prepare IRS Form 1099-NEC or 1099-MISC Reconcile accounts payable transactions and resolve invoice discrepancies or payment issues. Assist with month-end and year-end closing activities related to accounts payable. Prepare and maintain prepaid expense schedules and monthly amortization entries. Support fixed asset accounting, including asset additions, disposals, transfers, depreciation tracking, and inventory maintenance. Ensure compliance with internal controls, accounting standards, and institutional policies. Respond to vendor and campus community inquiries professionally and promptly. Assist with audits by providing requested documentation and reports. Generate reports and support process improvements for supplier invoice and expense processes within Workday and related financial systems. Responsible for tracking uncleared checks and reporting Abandoned Property to the State of New Hampshire. Perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or related field preferred. Minimum of 2 years of accounts payable or general accounting experience required. Experience using Workday financial systems strongly preferred. Knowledge of accounts payable processes, expense reimbursements, prepaid expenses, and fixed asset accounting. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other Microsoft Office applications. Commitment to confidentiality and high ethical standards.   Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education or nonprofit accounting. Familiarity with month-end close processes and audit support. Familiarity with electronic invoice and workflow systems   In order to be considered for this position, please submit both a resume and a cover letter. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    },
