    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Coordinator--Clinical-Placements-and-Partnerships_R1711": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Clinical Placements and Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a Coordinator, Clinical Placements and Partnerships for the Jean School of Nursing and Health Sciences.  This position coordinates clinical placements, experiential learning internships, and related activities for faculty and students across the Jean School of Nursing and Health Sciences. The Coordinator develops and maintains strong partnerships with healthcare and public health organizations to support high-quality student learning experiences. The position also collaborates closely with the Jean School Dean and Program Directors to assist with programmatic, operational and administrative activities in support of Jean School programs. The Coordinator, Clinical Placements and Partnerships is a 12-month calendar year position and reports directly to the Dean of the Jean School. Responsibilities: Clinical Rotation Assignments and Placements Coordinate clinical rotations, specialty experiences, observations, and undergraduate preceptorships across fall, winter, spring, and summer semesters. Coordinate student and faculty onboarding requirements for clinical placements, including health, safety, facility, EMR, and other site-specific requirements. Communicate clinical expectations and onboarding responsibilities to students and faculty. Undergraduate Preceptorship Placements Coordinate the undergraduate preceptorship application and placement process, including presentations, application timelines, resume and cover letter preparation, student advising, and placement submissions. Develop and maintain placement tracking systems and submit required documentation through the Centralized Clinical Placement (CCP) system and to external clinical partners. Ensure compliance with applicable state Board of Nursing requirements. Communicate placement assignments, deadlines, documentation, and onboarding requirements to students. Experiential Learning Internships Coordinate student experiential learning experiences with the Community & Public Health Program Director Submit required documentation through the Centralized Clinical Placement (CCP) system and to external partners. Ensure compliance with applicable institutional partner requirements. Communicate placement assignments, deadlines, documentation, and onboarding requirements to students. Health Requirements and Compliance Coordinate and monitor student compliance with drug screening, background checks, immunizations, BLS certification, FIT testing, and other clinical requirements. Maintain and monitor student compliance through CastleBranch and ensure accurate documentation of exemptions and required health records. Update health and immunization requirements in accordance with current CDC recommendations and facility requirements. Serve as a resource for students regarding health, immunization, and clinical compliance requirements. Coordinate onboarding and compliance requirements for Health Sciences internship students as assigned. Healthcare Partnerships and Affiliation Agreements Develop, establish, and maintain relationships with healthcare and public health organizations that provide clinical and internship experiences. Serve as the Jean School of Nursing and Health Sciences liaison to clinical partners and healthcare agencies. Initiate and coordinate affiliation agreements and contracts in collaboration with the Director. Seek new clinical opportunities and represent the nursing program at regional nursing and clinical placement meetings. Centralized Clinical Placement (CCP) Manage the Jean School's CCP account, including requesting, renewing, and updating clinical and preceptorship placements. Maintain accurate faculty, student, clinical site, schedule, and placement information within CCP and for non-CCP sites. Participate in regional CCP meetings and coordinate the annual CCP agreement. Student Support and Program Administration Collaborate with students, faculty, Health Services, Accessibility Resource Center, Athletics, Registrar, Career Development, and other College departments to address clinical placement, accommodation, and student support needs. Coordinate modified or alternative clinical placements in collaboration with appropriate College personnel and healthcare organizations. Assist with adjunct faculty and staff recruitment and onboarding activities. Respond to student, faculty, and healthcare organization inquiries and assist the Dean and Program Directors with additional programmatic and administrative responsibilities. Preferred Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree preferred; degree in nursing, healthcare, education, business, or a related field is desirable. Prior experience coordinating clinical, internship, or experiential learning placements required. Proficiency with Google Workspace and Microsoft Office; willingness and ability to learn and utilize additional technologies, including Centralized Clinical Placement (CCP), CastleBranch, and Canvas. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, projects, and deadlines in a fast-paced, highly collaborative environment. Familiarity with student affiliation agreements, healthcare partnerships, and contract processes preferred. Excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication, organizational, and customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective relationships with students, faculty, healthcare partners, and internal College departments. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college in advancing its Catholic identity and strategic priorities, which include institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Prevention-Education-Specialist_R1710": {
      "title": "Prevention Education Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in Benedictine tradition, is seeking a full-time, 11-month (June off) Prevention Education Specialist. The Prevention Education Specialist develops and implements campus-wide violence prevention education while serving as one of the College's designated Confidential Resource Advisors (CRA) for students impacted by sexual misconduct, relationship violence, domestic violence, stalking, and sexual harassment. Rooted in Saint Anselm College's Benedictine tradition, this position promotes a campus culture of hospitality, community, respect for the inherent dignity of every person, and care for the common good through evidence-informed prevention initiatives, outreach, and education. As one of the College's designated Confidential Resource Advisors, the Prevention Education Specialist provides confidential support, information, safety planning, and referrals, but does not conduct investigations or participate in disciplinary decision-making.   The position reports to the Director of Operations at The Harbor, the violence prevention office within Saint Anselm College Health Services, and collaborates with Student Affairs, Title IX, Athletics, Residence Life, Campus Safety, Counseling, faculty, staff, and community partners.   This position is supported by grant funding and is subject to the continued availability of funding.   Essential Duties and Responsibilities Prevention Education Develop, implement, and evaluate campus-wide violence prevention programs that foster respect, inclusion, belonging, and personal responsibility. Facilitate workshops on consent, healthy relationships, bystander intervention, sexual violence, dating and domestic violence, stalking, trauma-informed practices, and related topics. Coordinate awareness campaigns and outreach events that strengthen community and promote student well-being. Recruit and support peer educators and student leaders. Assess program effectiveness and maintain participation data.   Confidential Resource Services Serve as one of the College's designated Confidential Resource Advisor for students affected by interpersonal violence. Provide trauma-informed support, crisis intervention, safety planning, and resource referrals in a manner that honors each individual's dignity, autonomy, and lived experience. Explain reporting options, supportive measures, institutional processes, and community resources while respecting student choice. Accompany students to meetings or appointments, as appropriate. Maintain confidentiality in accordance with New Hampshire law and institutional policy.   Collaboration & Compliance Build collaborative relationships across campus and with community partners to advance a coordinated, compassionate response to interpersonal violence. Support compliance with the Clery Act, VAWA, Title IX education requirements, and applicable New Hampshire laws. Assist with grant-funded initiatives, assessment, and reporting.   Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in psychology, social work, counseling, public health, criminal justice, education, or a related field. Two years of experience in prevention education, higher education, victim services, counseling, public health, or a related field. Knowledge of trauma-informed practices and interpersonal violence prevention. Strong presentation, communication, and organizational skills.   Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education. Knowledge of Title IX, the Clery Act, VAWA, and New Hampshire Confidential Resource Advisor laws. Experience with grant-funded programs and program evaluation.   Successful candidates will be able to assist the college in advancing its Catholic identity and strategic priorities, which include institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Anselm/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Library-Technical-Assistant_R1708": {
      "title": "Library Technical Assistant  - Periodicals",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nGeisel Library at Saint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, seeks a part-time Periodicals Supervisor to join their team. This is a fall and spring semester (16 weeks each term) position. One-four shifts are available: Tuesday 5:30 p.m. – 12:00 a.m. Wednesday 5:30 p.m. - 12:00 am Saturday’s 6:00 p.m.– 11:00 p.m. Sunday 6 pm to 12:00 a.m. Candidates must complete the online application, and provide a cover letter, resume, and three references to be considered for the position. Job Duties The Periodicals Supervisor is responsible for managing all Periodical Desk operations during assigned hours and performs a variety of duties that include: checking out library materials using an automated library circulation and security system, supervising student assistants, aiding patrons with photocopying, scanning, and printing, maintenance of the library collection such as shelving materials and shelf reading, assisting with Interlibrary Loan request processing, assisting with the security of users and collections, opening/closing the library, and other projects as assigned. Additional evening and weekend hours may be possible throughout the academic year. Periodicals Supervisors are also cross-trained to provide supervision of Circulation Desk operations. Required Skills Able to work independently and follow directions Reliable and dependable attendance, including the ability to work during severe weather events Exceptional customer service and interpersonal skills Ability to resolve patron concerns and difficulties with tact, courtesy, and sound judgment Flexibility to assist in occasional coverage of other shifts Proven history of working in a team environment while maintaining a positive attitude Demonstrated capacity for embracing change and new initiatives, programs, and services Strong office and computer skills Ability to lift 30 pounds Required Experience An Associate degree plus 1-2 years of relevant experience, or the equivalent combination of education and experience. Desired Experience Supervisory experience Experience working with library computer systems, such as Sierra, LibGuides, and Illiad. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college in advancing its mission and strategic priorities , which includes institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    }
  },
